        "reflection": "Luke records twice that Mary treasured all these things in her heart — once after the shepherds came at Jesus' birth, and once after she found her twelve-year-old in the temple. Those are two completely different moments — the first is wonder, the second is fear melting into bewilderment. And in both, Mary does the same thing: she takes the moment inward, holds it, turns it over. I don't want you to miss what she doesn't do. She doesn't perform a certainty she doesn't have. She doesn't explain away what she can't understand. She just keeps it. What Luke is showing you is a kind of interior practice that's essential for anyone walking through mystery — and motherhood is full of mystery. You will have moments with your children you don't understand, can't explain, and can't resolve. The practice Mary models isn't passive resignation. It's active holding — bringing the unresolved thing before God and staying with it instead of demanding an answer. Every mother is carrying some Mary moment right now: something about her child, her calling, or God's plan that she can't make sense of. The invitation is the same one Mary took — treasure it, stay with it, and let God be the one who interprets it in time.",
